# 目的 (Purpose)

This repository is an llm_wiki-centered platform for automatic factor-based investment. It converts source documents to Markdown with AnyDoc, then turns that source material into durable, linked investment knowledge used to propose, calculate, review, and backtest factor expressions.

## 运行循环 (Operating Loop)

1. Preserve every input document byte-for-byte under `raw/sources/`.
2. Convert every supported input to Markdown under `wiki/sources/`, then analyze those pages with the configured LLM Wiki prompt.
3. Extract source-backed investment philosophies, universes, decision rules, portfolio and risk construction, horizons, execution, monitoring, and review methodologies.
4. Consolidate duplicate factor definitions while preserving formula and expression variants.
5. Link related factors, methodologies, evidence, and backtest experience.
6. Run factor calculation and backtesting through auditable control-plane goals and todos.
7. Write evidence and outcomes back into the wiki without silently overwriting active pages.
8. Analyze news from macro logic through industry transmission and fundamental valuation, publishing only evidence-complete opportunities that pass deterministic catalyst and valuation gates.

The wiki is the system's long-lived white knowledge and memory. Generated claims must remain traceable to sources, derived formulas must be labeled, unknowns must be explicit, and human-approved active content has authority over automated updates.
